Q: UI not updating during longPress A: <p>This is a tricky problem! The UI not updating during a long press in Detox tests is because of how Detox waits for the app to be &quot;idle&quot; before moving on.</p>
<h2>Why This Happens</h2>
<p>When you do a long press, Detox thinks the app is busy (because you're still touching the screen). So it waits until you stop touching before it checks for UI changes. That's why the UI seems &quot;frozen&quot; during the long press.</p>
<h2>Possible Fix: Use <code>element.longPressAndDrag</code></h2>
<p>One thing you could try is using <code>longPressAndDrag</code> with a very small drag distance. This might let the UI update:</p>
<pre><code>await element(by.id('your-element')).longPressAndDrag(
  35000,           // duration in ms
  0.5, 0.5,        // start position (center)
  element(by.id('your-element')),
  0.5, 0.5,        // end position (same spot)
  'slow'
);
</code></pre>
<h2>Another Option: Use <code>jest.setTimeout</code> and Manual Checks</h2>
<p>You could also break it into smaller steps:</p>
<pre><code>jest.setTimeout(60000); // give test more time

// Start the long press
await element(by.id('your-element')).tap();

// Wait and check UI at intervals
for (let i = 0; i &lt; 35; i++) {
  await new Promise(r =&gt; setTimeout(r, 1000)); // wait 1 second
  // Check if UI updated
  await expect(element(by.id('updating-text'))).toExist();
}
</code></pre>
<h2>It Might Be a Detox Limitation</h2>
<p>Honestly, this might just be how Detox works right now. The iOS simulator handles touch events differently than real devices, and Detox's sync system doesn't play well with very long press gestures.</p>
<p>If you find a solution that works, please share it here! I'd love to learn what worked for you.</p>

Q: How to point to other GMail accounts/folders in Google Apps Script A: <p>As I understand, you're trying to retrieve ten threads from other inbox accounts. Even though you have access to other users inbox as a delegate, to access the delegated accounts inbox data with the API, you need to authenticate as that specific user. There is a way to do this programmatically in Apps Script but this alternative works for Google Workspace accounts and you need administrator role to configure certain things in the Google Workspace Admin console.</p>
<p>For this you can use a Google Service account with domain-wide delegation and the email address of the user you are trying to impersonate.</p>
<p>You can use the following sample code, I used <a href="https://www.labnol.org/code/20375-service-accounts-google-apps-script" rel="nofollow noreferrer">this</a> as a reference and it works.</p>
<pre><code>var JSON = {
  private_key: 'private_key',
  client_email: 'client_email',
  client_id: 'client_id',
  user_email: 'email_address_of_user_to_impersonate',
};

function getOAuthService(user) {
  return OAuth2.createService('Service Account')
    .setTokenUrl('https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/token')
    .setPrivateKey(JSON.private_key)
    .setIssuer(JSON.client_email)
    .setSubject(JSON.user_email)
    .setPropertyStore(PropertiesService.getScriptProperties())
    .setParam('access_type', 'offline')
    .setScope('https://mail.google.com/');
}

function getUserThreads() {
  var service = getOAuthService();
  service.reset();
    var url = 'https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/'+JSON.user_email+'/threads?maxResults=10';
    var response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(url, {
      headers: {
        Authorization: 'Bearer ' + service.getAccessToken(),
      },
    });
    Logger.log(response.getContentText());
}

function reset() {
  var service = getOAuthService();
  service.reset();
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> You need to add the OAuth2 Library to your Apps Script project.</p>
<p><strong>References:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://support.google.com/a/answer/7378726" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Create a service account</a></li>
<li><a href="https://support.google.com/a/answer/162106?#zippy=%2Cbefore-you-begin%2Cset-up-domain-wide-delegation-for-a-client" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Manage Domain Wide Delegation</a></li>
<li><a href="https://developers.google.com/gmail/api/reference/rest/v1/users.threads/list" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Method: users.threads.list</a></li>
</ul>
